{
  "id": "church",
  "kind": "api",
  "title": "Breeze ChMS (gracechurch)",
  "description": "Breeze ChMS church database at gracechurch.breezechms.com: Pastoral care and giving reports",
  "credential": {
    "label": "Breeze API key",
    "description": "The church's API key from Breeze → Extensions → API (https://gracechurch.breezechms.com/extensions/api). It has no scopes: it reaches the whole account, giving included. The connector sends it only to gracechurch.breezechms.com.",
    "placeholder": "Paste Breeze API key"
  },
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Church records: profile-field decoding, occurrence/person joins, decimal giving, and archival API caveats.",
    "content": "# Breeze ChMS usage\n\nChurch database: gracechurch.breezechms.com.\n\nChurch purpose: Pastoral care and giving reports\n\nCalendar feed addresses and embed keys are always removed; profile details follow the requested vendor detail level.\n\n## Church records\n\nBreeze ChMS (now Tithely Church Management) holds people, tags, events,\nattendance, forms, volunteers and giving. People carry contact information,\nbirthdates and family ties; giving reveals donors and amounts. Reduce records\nin code and return only the names, counts or totals the task needs.\n\n## Ids and joins\n\nIds are numeric strings. Resolve them from the relevant inventory before\nwriting. Events have an occurrence id and a series `eventId`; attendance,\nvolunteers and check-in use the occurrence id. Event and pledge lists can lag\nup to 15 minutes behind the site. An all-zero MySQL date means no time was\nrecorded, including no check-out.\n\nProfile `details` use field ids, not names. Resolve field and option ids from\n`list_profile_fields`; multiple-choice filters join option ids with `-`.\nA person-name lookup requires listing people and matching in code. Form entry\nresponses similarly join to that form's field ids.\n\n## Giving\n\nGiving, funds and pledges use archival endpoints removed from the public\nreference in 2023. They can change or vanish without notice. Amounts are\nexact decimal strings: reduce them with integer-cent arithmetic, and read the\ncurrency from `get_account_summary`. A split gift's fund amounts belong to\nits fund ids. Tithe.ly deposits sync in batches, so recent gifts can be absent.\nEditing a giving transaction may return a new payment id.\nUse `limit: 1000` when reducing broad giving ranges: each local page refetches\nthe bounded vendor list, so larger windows avoid repeated full-list fetches.\n\n## Required sequences\n\nCheck for an existing person before adding one: creation does not deduplicate.\nResolve profile fields before updating them. Text, dates (M/D/YYYY) and option\nids use `response`; email, phone, address and family-role values use `details`.\nNamed person writes take these entries in `values`.\nFamily changes can remove previous associations. Attendance check-out records\na departure time; removing attendance deletes the record instead.\n\nBreeze sends writes as GET requests too. Query names ending in `_json` take\nJSON-encoded strings. The named person writes encode their typed profile values\nfor you. The account-log `object_json` is a serialized affected-object value;\nits free-text description has no stable schema. Events and account logs have\nvendor caps: narrow the date range when the result fills its limit.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** while `page.hasMore` is true, continue with `page.nextCursor` unchanged. For `breeze_api_details`, `breeze_api_search`, `list_attendance`, `list_contributions`, `list_funds`, `list_people`, `list_profile_fields`, `list_tags`, pass it as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw paging anchors on continuations. For `breeze_api_read`, put it in `query[page.param]` or `body[page.param]`, as `page.in` specifies. Keep the original method, path, filters, page size, fields and headers. Paged `list_*` and `search_*` reads take `limit` (default 100, at most 1000). The last page has no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation was withheld. When approaching execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor before the call that would exceed it and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `breeze_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `breeze_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `breeze_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `breeze_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. `not_found` means the record does not exist; this API tells absence from a permission gap. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.\n"
  },
